WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
OpenAI releases mathematical results from an internal frontier model in a public GitHub repository with lean formalizations and compute estimates. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 196. OpenAI released a broad range of new mathematical results produced by an internal frontier model. The company is publishing the results in a GitHub repository that includes formalizations of many proofs in lean. 10 summaries of the model's reasoning appear alongside estimations

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.360
of compute spent and statistics on attempted problems.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:39.560
The average result used the equivalent compute of roughly three hours of chat GPT Pro thinking.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:45.820
OpenAI consulted the independent advisory group on mathematics and artificial intelligence

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:49.540
at the Institute for Advanced Study to develop release protocols.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.040
The company is funding workshops around major AI-produced results.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:59.340
It states it is working to responsibly release the model that produced these results while

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:03.920
While continuing to evaluate internal frontier models on mathematics and other sciences,

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:08.840
the repository will be updated with more formalizations as they become available.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:14.040
Additional details about how the results were obtained are included to promote transparency.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:19.940
Future releases will focus on improving paper quality through better citations, exposition,

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:20.920
and presentation.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.780
Wave prune restricts each rope channel to its first rotation period.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:31.160
The method raises the helmet score on 4 of 5 tested models without extra tuning.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:37.800
One example shows an increase from 35.7 to 40.0 on QN38B.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:43.440
When pre-training from scratch, models using wave prune achieve lower validation loss at

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.440
extrapolated lengths.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:50.320
The approach induces fine-grained sparsity that hardware-aligned CUDA kernels exploit for

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:58.560
1.15 times pre-fill, and 1.24 times decoding speed-ups over flash attention, too, at 32,000

00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.020
context.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:07.820
Fiorello V0.5 is a 4-billion-parameter open-model fine-tuned on QN34B base, with low-rank

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.360
adapters and a decision-head.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:15.240
It targets the evidence inference 2.0 task of answering whether an intervention significantly

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.340
changed an outcome.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:24.240
On the test split of 1,218 prompts from 333 articles, it achieved an expected calibration

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.980
error of 0.0168.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:36.680
Macro F1 reached 0.9248, and log loss sat 0.1829 below Gemma 431 be it.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:43.360
The model was trained only on the 1,431 training articles whose licenses permit reuse.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:49.720
It was released under the Apache license 2.0 after passing four pre-registered criteria.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:56.800
Refusing directions concentrate in sparse component mechanisms comprising 28-48% of upstream

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:03.940
attention and MLP components. Those mechanisms retain 88-101% of steering effectiveness.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:09.960
Effective steering further concentrates in approximately 50% of residual stream dimensions.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:15.360
That concentration retains 85-98% of baseline performance.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:19.920
The study decomposes refusal steering across four open-weight models.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.980
All code and raw experimental results are released on GitHub.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:31.960
Low capacity reduces causal effectiveness by 84% and low responsiveness by 95%.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:37.660
CAGD retains a small set of old prompts and uses a frozen previous model to reconstruct

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:38.460
completions.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:42.340
It matches predictive distributions while learning the next task.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:49.040
On a 219 million mask diffusion language model, the method reduced four task final held

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:54.140
out loss from 2.927 to 1.114 in one task order.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:59.760
The same order in reverse dropped from 2.168 to 0.891.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:07.300
The soft targets lowered final average loss by 0.055 over hard replay when teacher generated

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:14.020
support was identical. The approach was tested on fresh facts and natural instructions across SMDM

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:21.080
and QN3. SONC reads option probabilities after every loop and trains each loop with a proper scoring

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:29.620
rule. One model therefore serves budgets from 1-8 loops. On 10,027 test decisions from 59 sources,

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.780
It reached 72.0% accuracy.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:38.340
That figure sits 13.5 points above a non-loop model of the same shape.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:44.840
On depth-controlled tasks, loops extend solvable depth beyond training depths where larger single-pass

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:45.700
models fail.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:51.260
Used as a judge for policy optimization with reinforcement learning and no-gold answers,

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:55.880
Sansi raised the generators F1 by 7.7 points.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:05:02.020
Refold removes two kinds of interturn redundancy by replacing earlier displayed content with

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:02.560
Stubbs.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.880
It also folds completed turns into one-line notes.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:12.320
The method reduces token consumption by up to 2.5 times and halves KV cache memory

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:12.980
per session.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:18.660
Those gains appear across five long horizon benchmarks and two frontier LLMs.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:23.940
Under capped context budgets, it avoids up to 92% of forced compactions.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:24.100
operations.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:30.440
Under concurrent serving workloads, it reduces request queuing delays by up to 100%.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:36.880
Inference accelerates by up to 1.7 times while cutting inference costs by up to 3.4 times.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:41.040
D-loop continues drafting while the draft model remains confident.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.080
It verifies all accumulated tokens together.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:49.920
Loop-aware training exposes the draft model to its own hidden states for unverified tokens.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:57.540
Caros Eagle 3, D-Flash, Domino, D-Spark, and Multitoken prediction modules, D-Loop improves

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:02.160
wall-clock speed up by 5-41% while preserving lossless decoding.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:09.580
Carote scores papers on 8 dimensions including statistical power, causal identification, pre-registration,

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:10.940
and conflict of interest.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:17.000
On 60 held out clinical trial documents, extracted information matched expert labels in

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:26.180
221 of 242 protocol scorepoints. It matched in 294 of 370 results publication scorepoints.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:30.460
The system links each judgment to the specific passage supporting it.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:36.080
It was applied to a corpus containing 3,913 randomized trial reports.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:43.140
Tied 2.0 runs an interchangeable recognizer and a keyed anonymizer on institution-owned hardware.

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:49.580
Dates receive a per-patient interval preserving offset. Each value receives the same surrogate

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:55.600
across all occurrences under a given key. On two gold annotated corpora, the default

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:04.120
configuration reached span level recall of 0.88 in domain. Recall reached 0.77 on an out-of-domain

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:07.960
Corpus at Precision 0.88 and 0.87.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:14.140
The engine is MIT licensed and the recognizer is available under a gated research use agreement.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:21.780
The Crosent minor benchmark comprises 602 papers, 102 carry human validated gold annotations

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:25.480
and 500 carry LLM generated silver annotations.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:30.640
The annotations cover the full Crosent schema, including responsible AI fields.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:34.420
single-pass extraction consistently outperformed for

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:38.400
agentech architectures. The largest gap appeared on long-form

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:41.540
RAI fields. The authors released the benchmark,

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:45.700
evaluation code, judge audit, live demo, and leaderboard.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:50.600
Accent CL extracts multi-layer representations from a frozen whisper

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:54.180
large V3 encoder. It applies an imbalance aware

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:58.700
cross entropy loss plus domain mean alignment loss. On a five-class

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:07.400
task it achieved 77.1% balanced accuracy and 76.9% macro averaged F1. Adding

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:13.440
Spanish accented English yielded 83.3% F1 on the new class while retaining

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:19.620
77.3% balanced accuracy on base classes. Subsequent addition of Chinese

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:27.500
accented English yielded 61.8% F1 on the new class while preserving 77.6% balanced

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:33.600
accuracy. Pop the hood on frontier model result sharing, and the engineering choice becomes clear.

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:40.240
Labs must decide whether to ship raw claims or add machine-checkable artifacts. Open AI

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:46.040
added lean formalizations so any researcher can run an automated checker. That step removes

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:51.600
the common failure mode where a textual proof later reveals subtle gaps. Compute accounting

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:54.700
accounting appears as chat GPT pro-hour equivalents.

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:59.660
Outsiders gain a rough sense of inference budget without proprietary training details.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:05.820
Explicit revision and citation protocols reduce the risk that later corrections become untraceable.

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:10.520
The extra formalization cost trades against the gain in external scrutiny.

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:16.200
When the goal is accelerating collective progress, the verifiable route sets the current practical

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:16.740
standard.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:23.600
Monitor the open AI mathematics GitHub repository for new lean formalizations and additional

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:25.380
result summaries as they are added.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:30.460
Review the published reasoning traces to understand how the frontier model structured its

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:31.640
mathematical arguments.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:38.980
Test wave prune on a rope-based model at 32,000 context to measure the reported pre-fill and

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:40.020
decoding speed-ups.

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:48.160
Evaluate Fiorello V0.5 on randomized trial articles under the Apache 2.0 license to check

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:50.940
calibration on your own evidence inference tasks.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:56.480
Further disclosures of major scientific advancements from internal frontier models are expected

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:58.300
as evaluation standards evolve.

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:04.300
Additional workshops and conferences on AI-produced mathematical results will be announced in the

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:04.940
coming months.

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:10.300
More class, incremental and continual learning frameworks for speech and language models are

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:13.500
likely as imbalance and domain shift robustness improve.

